---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const title = 'About — Trout';
const description =
  'Why Trout exists: the on-the-water decision tool that works offline and respects privacy. Built in the open as a small, deep v1 for Tennessee.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/about/">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Trout exists because the moment you actually need an answer on the water — <em>what is this
      bug, is this flow fishable, what got stocked?</em> — is usually the moment you have no cell
    signal and no patience for a 40-page forum thread.
  </p>

  <h2>The idea</h2>
  <p>
    Fishbrain owns community. TroutRoutes owns navigation and access. Nobody owns the
    <em>decision tool</em>: the structured bug key that runs with no signal, the fishability score
    that speaks English instead of CFS, and the stocking schedule that arrives weekly and honestly
    links its official source. That's the gap this project fills.
  </p>

  <h2>Principles we don't bend</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Offline-first.</strong> Every core feature works in airplane mode. Online data enhances; nothing core requires it.</li>
    <li><strong>Privacy by architecture.</strong> No accounts, no location uploads, no trackers. Not "we value your privacy" — we never take it.</li>
    <li><strong>Attribution culture.</strong> Every number on this site names its official source and tells you to verify there. We are a convenience layer, never the authority.</li>
    <li><strong>Small v1, deep not wide.</strong> One launch state (Tennessee), no lakes, no maps, no photo-AI, no social feed. Depth beats a half-finished atlas.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it's built</h2>
  <p>
    The site you're reading is static HTML — no JavaScript required to read any answer on it. The
    app is an installable PWA: the hatch key and scoring run as pure functions on your device, the
    offline payload is text and SVG line art, and the whole thing is sized to fit on a phone without
    asking forgiveness. Government data comes from the USGS and state wildlife agencies; the only
    server component is a small pipeline that keeps public snapshots fresh.
  </p>

  <h2>Roadmap discipline</h2>
  <p>
    The v1 out-list is binding and written down: no user accounts or social features, no lakes or
    maps, no paid tier yet, no ads beyond reserved placeholders, and nothing that ever uploads your
    location. The <a href="/blog/">launch notes</a> are where changes to that list get argued.
  </p>
</Base>
